1
00:04:26,666 --> 00:04:32,666
The Dalton Gang is a western film directed by Christopher Forbes.

2
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:59,333
When their brother Frank is killed by an outlaw, brothers Bob Dalton, Emmett
Dalton and Gray Dalton join their local sheriff's department.

3
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:26,000
When they are cheated by the law, they turn to crime, robbing trains and anything else
they can steal from over the course of two years in the early 1890's.

4
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:52,666
Trying to out do Jesse James, they attempt to rob two banks at
once in October of 1892, and things get ugly

5
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:19,333
Slade, played by William Adams.

6
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Bridget McGill, played by Jezibell Anat.

7
00:31:06,666 --> 00:31:12,666
Skeeter, played by Gunner Bridger.

8
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:39,333
Julia Johnson, played by Meghan Bridgers.

9
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Bob Dalton, played by Jerry Chesser.

10
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
Grat Dalton, played by Alan Cope II.

11
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Emmett Dalton (May 3, 1871 – July 13, 1937) was an American outlaw, train
robber and member of the Dalton Gang in the American Old West.

12
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Part of a gang that attempted to rob two banks in Coffeyville, Kansas, on October 5, 1892, he
was the only member of five to survive, despite receiving 23 gunshot wounds.

13
00:57:46,666 --> 00:57:52,666
Two of his brothers were killed.

14
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
After serving 14 years in prison for the crime, Dalton was pardoned.

15
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
He later capitalized on his notoriety, both as a writer and as an actor.

16
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
His 1918 serial story Beyond the Law was adapted as a
like-named silent film in which he played himself.

17
01:15:33,333 --> 01:15:39,333
His 1931 book When the Daltons Rode was adapted after his
death as a 1940 film of the same name.
